<title>UK: Vegetable oil, sugar carriers collide off Malta.</title>
<headline>Vegetable oil, sugar carriers collide off Malta.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish-flag Villa, with a cargo of sugar, and the Panama-flag Ginga Eagle, laden with vegetable oil, are being inspected following a collision off Malta, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Part of the cargo of the 16,530 dwt Villa, bound for Israel, had been damaged.</p>
<p>The 19,683 dwt Ginga Eagle was bound for France.</p>
